#Writing and Executing our First Terraform Script:

•Step-by-Step Environment Setup
•Provision Infrastructure: Create an EC2 VM with basic configurations (or as per your requirement) via the AWS Console.
•Establish Connection: Connect using an SSH connection on your terminal and follow the sequence below:

~ Install terraform using the command from developer.hashicorp.com
~ Create a dedicated working directory
sudo mkdir terraform-01-script

~ Set your active session security credentials
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="xyz"
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="xyz"

~ Navigate into your directory and verify contents
cd terraform-01-script
ls -l

~ Create and open your first configuration file in Vim
vi tf-script-1.tf

#Configuration File Code (tf-script-1.tf)

•Press i to enter Insert Mode in Vim and add the following infrastructure code:

provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
}

resource "aws_instance" "linux_vm" {
  ami             = "ami-05d4604467837b4ec"
  instance_type   = "t2.micro"
  key_name        = "Ankush-Key-Pair"
  security_groups = ["default"]

  tags = {
    Name = "Ankush-Server"
  }
}

•Press Esc followed by :wq to save and exit Vim.

#Execution Steps
We need to run the deployment lifecycle commands in sequence within our workspace:

terraform init
terraform fmt
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve

*Result: After completion of the above steps, we will notice an EC2 instance named "Ankush-Server" successfully created in your AWS account console.
